WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.160
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.260 --> 00:02.190
[The characters, behaviors, locations, organizations, professions,

3
00:02.210 --> 00:04.140
and events depicted in this series are entirely fictional

4
00:04.160 --> 00:06.150
and created for entertainment purposes only.

5
00:06.170 --> 00:08.100
No harm or illegal action is intended to be promoted or encouraged.

6
00:08.120 --> 00:09.990
Viewer discretion is advised.]

7
00:10.020 --> 00:11.550
For this MV...

8
00:11.570 --> 00:13.550
you'll be the director once again, Jaab.

9
00:13.570 --> 00:15.160
The mood of the song is very sad,

10
00:15.250 --> 00:16.960
so I want somewhere that feels

11
00:16.980 --> 00:17.760
lonely and isolated.

12
00:17.780 --> 00:18.840
You can visit my house.

13
00:18.980 --> 00:19.440
Huh?!

14
00:19.760 --> 00:21.260
My house there has a lot of isolated corners.

15
00:21.400 --> 00:23.160
Can I really go there?

16
00:24.980 --> 00:26.770
Your hair is too long.

17
00:26.790 --> 00:29.620
It was getting in your eyes, so I wanted to brush it away.

18
00:29.660 --> 00:31.590
Why would that bother you?

19
00:31.610 --> 00:33.520
It did bother me, because I was looking...

20
01:29.030 --> 01:29.850
Jane.

21
01:30.490 --> 01:32.620
I'm too scared to scrub it any harder.

22
01:33.040 --> 01:34.900
I'm afraid your skin might come off.

23
01:39.200 --> 01:39.930
Brats,

24
01:39.950 --> 01:41.720
both you and the marker.

25
01:44.500 --> 01:45.410
Fine, fine.

26
01:45.740 --> 01:47.110
I guess I'm a brat, then.

27
01:50.890 --> 01:52.040
Cut it out already, Jane.

28
01:52.060 --> 01:53.120
You'll scrape yourself.

29
01:55.480 --> 01:57.000
How do I get home unnoticed now?

30
01:58.890 --> 01:59.760
You'll be fine.

31
01:59.860 --> 02:00.720
Trust me,

32
02:00.800 --> 02:02.530
no one actually cares that much.

33
02:04.050 --> 02:04.860
Mm.

34
02:08.890 --> 02:09.510
How about...

35
02:09.850 --> 02:10.720
you wear a face mask?

36
02:12.160 --> 02:12.720
Here.

37
02:13.710 --> 02:14.990
The mark is on my forehead.

38
02:15.010 --> 02:16.560
How would this help, Jaab?

39
02:19.530 --> 02:21.150
It definitely helps, Jane!

40
02:21.170 --> 02:22.120
Put it on like this.

41
02:22.620 --> 02:23.360
See?

42
02:24.060 --> 02:25.760
There! How about that, Jane?

43
02:25.780 --> 02:27.320
With this, I assure you.

44
02:27.340 --> 02:28.370
No one will see it

45
02:28.390 --> 02:29.560
for sure.

46
02:30.260 --> 02:31.280
Ow, Jane!

47
02:33.100 --> 02:34.280
That hurt.

48
02:45.710 --> 02:46.360
Jane.

49
02:48.230 --> 02:48.820
Here.

50
02:48.840 --> 02:49.660
For you.

51
02:56.680 --> 02:57.750
I don't need it.

52
02:59.190 --> 03:00.080
Oh, why not?

53
03:00.410 --> 03:01.860
Wear it, Jane.

54
03:03.380 --> 03:04.770
It smells really nice, and...

55
03:04.790 --> 03:06.680
it's got a hood to hide that forehead of yours.

56
03:07.400 --> 03:07.940
Take it.

57
03:08.130 --> 03:09.040
It smells very nice.

58
03:25.020 --> 03:25.680
Ow! Jeez...

59
03:26.070 --> 03:26.640
Ow...

60
03:26.730 --> 03:27.470
It's you

61
03:27.510 --> 03:28.220
who has a big forehead.

62
03:28.590 --> 03:29.350
Come on.

63
03:31.500 --> 03:32.390
Wait, Jane.

64
03:32.580 --> 03:33.200
What are you doing?

65
03:33.420 --> 03:34.080
I'm changing, obviously.

66
03:34.200 --> 03:35.320
Go change in the bathroom.

67
03:35.420 --> 03:36.360
You can't do it here.

68
03:36.460 --> 03:38.040
It's fine. Nobody is around.

69
03:38.060 --> 03:38.890
But I'm here!

70
03:38.910 --> 03:40.060
It's okay. I don't mind.

71
03:40.080 --> 03:41.940
But I do mind, Jane! Please!

72
03:41.960 --> 03:43.500
- It's okay, Jaab. - No, don't! No, Jane!

73
03:43.520 --> 03:45.220
- Please don't, Jane. - So we can finally head home.

74
03:45.240 --> 03:46.500
Go change in the bathroom, please.

75
03:46.520 --> 03:47.360
- Jane! - Jaab!

76
03:47.380 --> 03:47.960
No!

77
03:48.110 --> 03:49.080
I can see everything!

78
03:49.100 --> 03:50.060
Ah, Jane! I can see everything!

79
03:50.120 --> 03:51.560
Jane!!

80
03:53.240 --> 03:55.020
So much for a forehead makeover.

81
04:16.480 --> 04:19.440
This brat would like to say sorry. Forgive me.

82
04:23.190 --> 04:26.460
Once again, the chemistry between us grows stronger

83
04:26.920 --> 04:28.630
to the point where it triggers a reaction

84
04:28.660 --> 04:31.500
that makes my heart feel like it might burst.

85
06:21.380 --> 06:22.990
I think I've settled in.

86
06:25.830 --> 06:28.240
Has anyone been picking on you at the new company?

87
06:28.530 --> 06:29.680
New?

88
06:29.700 --> 06:31.280
I've been working here for months now.

89
06:31.300 --> 06:32.440
It's been almost a year already.

90
06:33.880 --> 06:36.000
Right. I forgot.

91
06:36.340 --> 06:39.640
It feels like you just left yesterday.

92
06:39.890 --> 06:41.130
Min, don't be so dramatic.

93
06:41.150 --> 06:42.250
I'm a grown-up, okay?

94
06:43.900 --> 06:46.840
So, has anyone been picking on you?

95
06:47.290 --> 06:48.200
I don't think so.

96
06:51.730 --> 06:56.090
And, like... has anyone been hitting on you?

97
07:01.450 --> 07:02.390
Maybe.

98
07:04.920 --> 07:05.570
Whoa...

99
07:05.590 --> 07:07.170
I think they need to get a new coach, Khanoon.

100
07:07.190 --> 07:07.840
Yeah.

101
07:07.860 --> 07:09.500
They're screwed if they don't.

102
07:09.520 --> 07:10.280
Watching them is a waste of time.

103
07:10.300 --> 07:12.000
I couldn't fucking sleep at all. Damn it.

104
07:15.520 --> 07:16.460
Sheesh.

105
07:16.480 --> 07:18.400
So, our sweet manager

106
07:18.420 --> 07:20.120
clocks in early today?

107
07:20.170 --> 07:20.840
Look.

108
07:20.860 --> 07:23.190
These mangoes from Jane's garden house

109
07:23.210 --> 07:24.010
taste wonderful!

110
07:24.030 --> 07:24.760
Here. Try some.

111
07:26.940 --> 07:27.650
Hm!

112
07:27.670 --> 07:28.500
How is it?

113
07:28.930 --> 07:30.280
It's really good!

114
07:32.200 --> 07:33.040
Told you.

115
07:34.430 --> 07:35.340
And...

116
07:35.570 --> 07:37.520
Will I get to eat a fresh one tomorrow?

117
07:38.010 --> 07:38.580
Yeah.

118
07:38.600 --> 07:39.560
Whoa, really?!

119
07:39.680 --> 07:40.910
Is there anything else

120
07:40.930 --> 07:42.200
that I can try at your orchard?

121
07:43.360 --> 07:44.280
It's packed.

122
07:44.660 --> 07:45.460
Whoa...

123
07:45.530 --> 07:46.240
Hey,

124
07:46.310 --> 07:46.970
Jaab.

125
07:47.090 --> 07:49.910
I heard that you'll be looking for inspirations at Jane's garden house?

126
07:51.090 --> 07:52.380
Yes, Sis.

127
07:52.400 --> 07:53.890
Marvelous!

128
07:53.910 --> 07:55.400
He's helping us cut costs.

129
07:55.740 --> 07:57.650
- You're such a sweetheart. - Whoa, Sis...

130
07:58.130 --> 07:59.760
Please put the knife down first,

131
08:01.950 --> 08:02.720
or else

132
08:02.880 --> 08:05.320
you'll end up nicking this handsome face.

133
08:06.450 --> 08:07.400
Right!

134
08:09.820 --> 08:10.370
Hey.

135
08:10.650 --> 08:12.470
Are you helping the company save money

136
08:12.490 --> 08:14.470
or are you supporting someone's business here?

137
08:14.640 --> 08:16.180
Damn you, Khanoon...

138
08:16.200 --> 08:16.720
Jaab.

139
08:16.790 --> 08:17.560
Yes? What is it?

140
08:19.890 --> 08:21.120
Sheesh...

141
08:21.430 --> 08:23.720
Your voice is softer.

142
08:25.550 --> 08:27.240
I think you're probably hungry.

143
08:28.660 --> 08:30.650
If you can't shut up, just eat this.

144
08:30.670 --> 08:31.480
- There! - What the hell?

145
08:33.280 --> 08:33.890
Uh...

146
08:34.180 --> 08:35.740
Your hoodie isn't completely dry yet.

147
08:35.760 --> 08:36.660
Do you need it tomorrow?

148
08:36.680 --> 08:37.840
I'll put it in my luggage.

149
08:38.240 --> 08:39.310
It's fine, Jane.

150
08:39.440 --> 08:40.360
I've got a couple more.

151
08:40.420 --> 08:42.040
I don't want to take up your space.

152
08:43.020 --> 08:44.560
It'll be cold at night, though.

153
08:45.020 --> 08:46.640
Bring some warm clothes to keep you cozy.

154
08:47.020 --> 08:47.600
Okay.

155
08:47.940 --> 08:48.980
Got it.

156
08:49.250 --> 08:49.970
By the way...

157
08:49.990 --> 08:51.920
when do you want me to pick you up tomorrow?

158
08:52.550 --> 08:53.660
Around 7-8 A.M., maybe?

159
08:53.680 --> 08:54.960
We'll arrive there at noon.

160
08:56.380 --> 08:56.960
Okay.

161
08:59.840 --> 09:01.840
Don't forget to pick me up, too.

162
09:04.080 --> 09:05.170
Wasn't the sticky rice enough?

163
09:05.190 --> 09:06.040
Shut it!

164
09:06.580 --> 09:07.550
You ruined the moment.

165
09:10.980 --> 09:12.480
These mangoes are super yummy.

166
09:12.550 --> 09:13.920
Bring me some more, if you don't mind.

167
09:13.940 --> 09:15.340
- Sure thing. - I want my parents to enjoy them, too.

168
09:15.360 --> 09:17.040
- Sure. - They like mangoes.

169
09:17.060 --> 09:17.890
Hey.

170
09:17.910 --> 09:19.130
I'm first.

171
09:19.150 --> 09:20.120
I'm first in line.

172
09:29.940 --> 09:31.000
Whoa, what?!

173
09:31.020 --> 09:32.120
Whoa, Jaab!

174
09:32.240 --> 09:34.490
What the hell is wrong with you? Why did you take me here?

175
09:34.510 --> 09:35.480
Let go! What is it?

176
09:35.790 --> 09:36.720
What the hell are you doing?

177
09:36.870 --> 09:38.160
Tell me what you know.

178
09:39.740 --> 09:40.320
Know what?

179
09:40.380 --> 09:41.720
You're acting like you do.

180
09:41.810 --> 09:43.440
Tell me what I know, then!

181
09:43.560 --> 09:45.640
Don't even try to trick me, asshole.

182
09:45.760 --> 09:47.580
What the hell are you talking about, exactly?

183
09:47.600 --> 09:48.480
Asshole?

184
09:49.590 --> 09:50.780
It's Jane.

185
09:50.800 --> 09:51.480
I mean...

186
09:51.610 --> 09:52.920
I'm talking about Jane.

187
09:53.390 --> 09:54.720
Oh...

188
09:55.100 --> 09:56.640
Jane...

189
09:57.320 --> 09:57.960
What about him?

190
09:58.620 --> 10:00.040
Uh, well...

191
10:02.080 --> 10:04.430
It's about me going to his place...

192
10:04.740 --> 10:07.020
He invited me himself, so don't take it the wrong way.

193
10:07.060 --> 10:07.860
Jane's house

194
10:07.880 --> 10:09.540
has a massive orchard

195
10:09.560 --> 10:10.660
and tons of hills.

196
10:10.680 --> 10:13.300
And people can visit and walk around.

197
10:13.320 --> 10:14.800
It's not just the two of us.

198
10:15.230 --> 10:18.020
Oh... I see.

199
10:18.040 --> 10:19.520
- Mm. - And?

200
10:20.520 --> 10:21.120
And...

201
10:21.760 --> 10:22.560
And...

202
10:23.790 --> 10:25.860
The reason I speak more softly around Jane

203
10:25.880 --> 10:27.020
is because he's small.

204
10:27.040 --> 10:29.380
I don't want to be loud and startle him.

205
10:29.400 --> 10:30.250
Small?

206
10:30.620 --> 10:31.990
He's only this tiny.

207
10:32.200 --> 10:33.360
The size of a bottle?

208
10:35.140 --> 10:35.780
He's like...

209
10:35.800 --> 10:37.220
- He's only this tiny, you see. - Oh.

210
10:37.240 --> 10:37.920
- Like... - This tiny?

211
10:38.400 --> 10:40.120
And his eyes twinkle.

212
10:40.330 --> 10:41.500
When he smiles...

213
10:41.630 --> 10:42.640
he smiles broadly

214
10:43.030 --> 10:44.400
almost from ear to ear.

215
10:44.750 --> 10:45.440
Also...

216
10:45.600 --> 10:47.670
his teeth are perfectly aligned.

217
10:47.690 --> 10:48.350
Seeing them makes me...

218
10:48.370 --> 10:50.540
want to see him every morning.

219
10:50.560 --> 10:51.520
Do you like Jane?

220
10:54.240 --> 10:55.020
I...

221
10:55.880 --> 10:56.560
like Jane...

222
10:58.430 --> 10:59.280
Right?

223
11:02.800 --> 11:03.640
Do I?

224
11:06.240 --> 11:07.440
How would I know?

225
11:08.340 --> 11:10.160
What should I do, Khanoon?

226
11:10.520 --> 11:11.840
I've never felt this way.

227
11:13.640 --> 11:15.440
When you're sure about it,

228
11:15.640 --> 11:16.980
tell me later.

229
11:17.380 --> 11:19.320
And I'll help you out.

230
11:19.810 --> 11:21.030
I know that

231
11:21.290 --> 11:23.540
a clueless loser like you

232
11:23.560 --> 11:24.960
can't make a move on your own.

233
11:27.830 --> 11:28.760
What do I have to do, then?

234
11:29.570 --> 11:31.040
Be sure about it first.

235
11:31.150 --> 11:32.320
That's it. I'll get going now.

236
11:32.340 --> 11:33.040
Wait!

237
11:33.180 --> 11:33.790
See you.

238
11:33.810 --> 11:35.430
Talk to me when you're sure enough.

239
11:35.450 --> 11:36.270
Damn it!

240
11:39.720 --> 11:41.090
Do I really have a crush on Jane?

241
11:41.440 --> 11:42.700
Or do I just think that he's adorable?

242
11:42.720 --> 11:44.600
Which means you have a crush on him, idiot!

243
11:44.910 --> 11:47.000
Let's go. I've got tons of unfinished tasks to take care of.

244
11:47.020 --> 11:48.440
Not just me, but you as well.

245
11:48.910 --> 11:50.320
Right. I'll join you soon.

246
11:54.360 --> 11:55.760
Damn it, Jaab!

247
12:00.500 --> 12:01.940
Thinking that he's adorable means I have a crush on him?

248
12:04.870 --> 12:05.770
Do I, though?

249
12:07.000 --> 12:08.170
Somebody like me?

250
12:08.200 --> 12:11.150
Come on, Jaab!

251
12:13.200 --> 12:14.000
Gosh...

252
12:14.580 --> 12:16.160
Why the hell is this stuff so complicated?

253
12:23.370 --> 12:23.980
Oh.

254
12:24.990 --> 12:25.770
Mek?

255
12:26.120 --> 12:27.010
What brings you here?

256
12:29.580 --> 12:30.650
Who's Jane?

257
12:35.790 --> 12:37.170
Whoa.

258
12:37.900 --> 12:39.650
Khanoon, you bastard.

259
12:39.670 --> 12:41.720
He can't keep a secret to save his life, huh?

260
12:42.210 --> 12:43.080
Come on, Jaab.

261
12:43.100 --> 12:44.960
Have you forgotten our group's motto?

262
12:45.030 --> 12:47.160
"Nothing is a personal matter,

263
12:47.330 --> 12:49.080
for it is always our matter."

264
12:49.350 --> 12:50.650
Yay!

265
12:51.800 --> 12:52.680
Yay...

266
12:54.710 --> 12:56.040
It's just the three of us.

267
12:56.400 --> 12:58.300
Can you even call that a group?

268
12:58.690 --> 12:59.660
For me,

269
12:59.680 --> 13:01.840
it's a group if there are more than two people.

270
13:05.540 --> 13:06.760
Hey, hey, Mek.

271
13:06.810 --> 13:07.760
Hey, what the fuck are you doing?!

272
13:07.830 --> 13:08.630
Mek, give it to me!

273
13:08.650 --> 13:09.840
Mek, Mek, Mek.

274
13:09.920 --> 13:11.100
- You... - Adorable.

275
13:11.120 --> 13:11.720
Hey!

276
13:13.800 --> 13:15.200
Cut it out, damn it.

277
13:15.240 --> 13:16.370
One picture, that's it.

278
13:17.260 --> 13:18.300
Become his boyfriend first

279
13:18.320 --> 13:19.540
before you get possessive, my guy.

280
13:19.560 --> 13:20.600
Don't jump the gun.

281
13:20.960 --> 13:21.700
His boyfriend?

282
13:25.310 --> 13:26.180
His boyfriend?

283
13:29.400 --> 13:31.760
You've lost it, just like what Khanoon told me.

284
13:33.410 --> 13:33.950
What?

285
13:35.000 --> 13:35.720
And look at you.

286
13:36.070 --> 13:37.480
You didn't tell me that you were back.

287
13:43.380 --> 13:46.200
I took my dog to the vet nearby, so I decided to swing by.

288
13:46.560 --> 13:48.080
Mon needs to be hospitalized.

289
13:49.870 --> 13:51.120
So you want to crash here for free?

290
13:51.710 --> 13:52.980
Come on.

291
13:53.000 --> 13:55.720
Your place is close to my dog's go-to hospital.

292
13:56.080 --> 13:57.680
It's for the sake of my dog, alright?

293
13:57.710 --> 13:59.530
I'm not crashing here for free, though.

294
13:59.970 --> 14:00.810
This is in exchange for...

295
14:00.840 --> 14:02.720
some relationship advice from me.

296
14:05.510 --> 14:06.480
Did I ask for it?

297
14:09.490 --> 14:10.800
But I'm actually surprised that

298
14:10.990 --> 14:12.560
a goofball like you

299
14:12.730 --> 14:14.860
is invested in a relationship.

300
14:14.880 --> 14:16.790
Invested, my ass.

301
14:17.150 --> 14:18.120
I just...

302
14:18.810 --> 14:19.690
Just what?

303
14:20.990 --> 14:21.920
My heart just...

304
14:22.990 --> 14:23.920
quivers a little.

305
14:23.950 --> 14:25.640
Quivers a little?

306
14:25.660 --> 14:27.100
But you're about to haul your ass

307
14:27.120 --> 14:29.360
out of the city to stay at his house?

308
14:30.150 --> 14:31.000
Yeah!

309
14:31.150 --> 14:32.240
But I have a reason for it.

310
14:32.400 --> 14:33.520
I'm heading there for work.

311
14:33.680 --> 14:35.080
And I'm warning you.

312
14:35.510 --> 14:37.080
What you heard from Khanoon

313
14:37.110 --> 14:38.600
needs to be taken with a grain of salt.

314
14:39.820 --> 14:41.360
You don't need to remind me.

315
14:41.380 --> 14:42.480
I took it with a grain of salt,

316
14:42.610 --> 14:44.110
but I can see hearts

317
14:44.240 --> 14:45.440
in your eyes.

318
14:45.550 --> 14:46.100
Wait...

319
14:49.960 --> 14:50.980
You're talking nonsense.

320
14:53.040 --> 14:54.060
Love

321
14:54.080 --> 14:55.640
isn't that intimidating.

322
14:55.750 --> 14:56.720
Trust me.

323
14:58.840 --> 15:00.760
I'm too scared to think about it.

324
15:02.110 --> 15:03.160
Give it a try.

325
15:13.510 --> 15:15.860
Khanoon said you're heading to Jane's place tomorrow, right?

326
15:15.880 --> 15:16.570
Yeah.

327
15:17.040 --> 15:18.840
Jane said it'd be cold at night,

328
15:19.010 --> 15:20.970
so I'm preparing some warm clothes.

329
15:26.080 --> 15:28.180
You told me to bring some warm clothes,

330
15:28.970 --> 15:30.670
but now you're shivering yourself?

331
15:35.110 --> 15:36.310
And...

332
15:37.720 --> 15:39.920
Would it keep me warm if I hugged you?

333
15:52.470 --> 15:53.320
How is it?

334
15:54.290 --> 15:55.950
Is the jacket as warm as me?

335
16:06.070 --> 16:07.650
Does Jane live near the North Pole or what?

336
16:10.900 --> 16:11.840
What do you mean?!

337
16:13.220 --> 16:14.600
North Pole, my ass.

338
16:15.430 --> 16:17.120
You said you'd go to his place,

339
16:17.150 --> 16:19.240
then you took out a down jacket.

340
16:19.290 --> 16:21.120
I thought it would be snowing there or something.

341
16:24.160 --> 16:24.690
Well...

342
16:25.390 --> 16:26.840
It's in Phetchabun.

343
16:27.290 --> 16:29.960
And you're wearing a down jacket there?

344
16:32.030 --> 16:32.990
None of your business.

345
16:35.760 --> 16:37.810
Has love destroyed your IQ, my friend?

346
16:37.830 --> 16:38.390
Wait.

347
16:39.010 --> 16:40.510
This isn't my blazer.

348
16:41.000 --> 16:42.290
It's fucking Jeng's.

349
16:42.490 --> 16:44.060
The maid must've taken the wrong one.

350
16:45.670 --> 16:46.290
Hey.

351
16:50.270 --> 16:51.160
How about you put it on?

352
16:51.630 --> 16:53.860
Try something new and make an impression.

353
17:01.340 --> 17:03.000
Jaab, you look absolutely stunning.

354
17:03.870 --> 17:05.830
You're too kind, Jane.

355
17:07.210 --> 17:08.080
Ready?

356
17:08.410 --> 17:09.000
Mm.

357
17:09.520 --> 17:10.160
Here.

358
17:10.440 --> 17:11.290
Alright, Jane!

359
17:11.350 --> 17:12.700
- That one, Jaab. There. - Which one?

360
17:12.720 --> 17:14.320
Yes, get it. Come on.

361
17:14.340 --> 17:15.260
Yes, that one.

362
17:15.300 --> 17:16.230
This one, Jane?

363
17:16.250 --> 17:17.230
- Yes, that one. - Okay.

364
17:17.250 --> 17:19.330
- Get it. Harder, harder. Come on. - Just a moment.

365
17:19.350 --> 17:20.800
Great job, Jaab. You're amazing.

366
17:23.790 --> 17:24.680
Honestly,

367
17:24.950 --> 17:26.400
don't try to act tough.

368
17:27.040 --> 17:29.800
I know how badly this trip messes with your heart.

369
17:33.060 --> 17:34.880
Will Jane know that I like him?

370
17:35.160 --> 17:37.200
If he finds out and hates me,

371
17:37.220 --> 17:38.200
what should I do?

372
17:39.320 --> 17:39.920
No.

373
17:40.140 --> 17:41.280
I do like him, don't I?

374
17:41.730 --> 17:42.720
I guess...

375
17:44.070 --> 17:44.960
Damn it, Jaab!

376
17:45.020 --> 17:46.600
Why did I fall for him?!

377
17:46.620 --> 17:48.190
Oh, my God! Damn it!

378
17:48.210 --> 17:49.320
Why...? Damn it!

379
17:49.340 --> 17:50.630
Why do I have feelings for him?!

380
17:53.160 --> 17:54.170
Mek, help me!

381
17:54.190 --> 17:55.490
Help me, damn it.

382
17:55.510 --> 17:57.830
Oh, my God!

383
18:05.630 --> 18:06.680
Did I keep you waiting?

384
18:06.700 --> 18:07.560
Oh, Jane.

385
18:09.870 --> 18:10.640
Whoa, Jane.

386
18:10.660 --> 18:11.970
Your bag is so small.

387
18:12.080 --> 18:14.150
I've got a ton of stuff on me.

388
18:14.170 --> 18:15.520
Mine looks so over-prepared.

389
18:15.610 --> 18:16.620
Not really.

390
18:17.240 --> 18:19.200
You're preparing to stay at another place.

391
18:19.290 --> 18:21.520
But that other place is my home. My stuff is already there.

392
18:22.780 --> 18:23.720
Right, right, right.

393
18:23.880 --> 18:25.690
Give it to me. I'll load it in the trunk.

394
18:40.650 --> 18:41.920
Your bag...

395
18:42.140 --> 18:43.440
is just as tiny as you, isn't it?

396
18:44.870 --> 18:45.490
Mm.

397
18:46.420 --> 18:47.280
It's like...

398
18:47.650 --> 18:48.830
your pen.

399
18:49.370 --> 18:50.550
Your pen is a brat, just like you.

400
18:51.800 --> 18:53.400
Right at the start of this trip?

401
19:04.000 --> 19:05.210
What are you waiting for? Come on.

402
19:07.030 --> 19:07.860
Jaab.

403
19:08.350 --> 19:10.040
You need to make it back here in one piece, okay?

404
19:11.230 --> 19:12.270
Come on!

405
19:13.080 --> 19:13.830
Hurry.

406
19:24.360 --> 19:25.440
Jaab, have you eaten?

407
19:28.830 --> 19:31.360
That's a single serving, so don't pretend like you care.

408
19:32.670 --> 19:33.260
Well, this.

409
19:33.750 --> 19:34.650
I made this one for you.

410
19:35.680 --> 19:36.320
Seriously?

411
19:37.220 --> 19:38.090
Fine, fine.

412
19:38.170 --> 19:39.290
Since you made it for me,

413
19:39.450 --> 19:40.160
I'll eat it.

414
19:42.890 --> 19:43.440
Here.

415
19:44.110 --> 19:45.120
Thank you.

416
19:47.490 --> 19:48.040
Hey!

417
19:48.060 --> 19:48.440
Whoa!

418
19:50.160 --> 19:51.380
Why did you hit me, Jane?

419
19:51.400 --> 19:53.560
You're driving. Why did you let go?

420
19:54.430 --> 19:55.720
It's on autopilot, Jane.

421
19:55.840 --> 19:57.110
It's a new feature.

422
19:57.240 --> 19:57.740
Cool, right?

423
19:57.760 --> 19:59.540
Dangerous. Don't do that again!

424
19:59.560 --> 20:01.920
It's a danger both to you and to others on the road.

425
20:02.680 --> 20:03.830
Right.

426
20:04.150 --> 20:05.480
I won't do it again.

427
20:06.890 --> 20:08.520
Don't pull that face.

428
20:08.540 --> 20:10.280
I know that you haven't learned your lesson.

429
20:11.190 --> 20:12.400
Come on, Jane.

430
20:12.420 --> 20:13.610
What should I do, then?

431
20:14.120 --> 20:15.920
I can't let go, so how am I supposed to eat?

432
20:18.070 --> 20:18.630
Here.

433
20:20.040 --> 20:20.590
Mm.

434
20:20.850 --> 20:22.200
This works, though.

435
20:28.780 --> 20:30.260
Oh, so good!

436
20:30.280 --> 20:31.000
Jaab.

437
20:31.500 --> 20:33.160
- Chew before you talk. - Chew before you talk.

438
20:34.690 --> 20:35.280
Mm.

439
20:35.620 --> 20:38.000
Do you need to choke to learn your lesson?

440
20:38.510 --> 20:40.590
"Do you need to choke to..."

441
20:44.230 --> 20:44.850
Jane.

442
20:46.540 --> 20:47.360
I'm choking.

443
20:48.940 --> 20:49.870
Thank you, Jane.

444
20:50.400 --> 20:51.200
Jane!

445
20:52.160 --> 20:53.600
Jane, I need water...

446
20:56.520 --> 20:57.280
Emergency.

447
20:57.320 --> 20:58.460
Help me, Jane!

448
20:59.340 --> 21:00.630
Jane!!

449
21:02.800 --> 21:03.950
Whoa, gentle, gentle.

450
21:03.970 --> 21:04.960
Gentle!

451
21:06.820 --> 21:07.660
Goodness...

452
21:09.080 --> 21:10.480
Were you that thirsty, dear?

453
21:10.520 --> 21:12.600
I'm sorry, Jane's mom...

454
21:13.690 --> 21:14.580
This is Auntie Kaew.

455
21:14.600 --> 21:15.320
She's my caretaker.

456
21:16.120 --> 21:17.630
I'm so sorry, Sis.

457
21:17.650 --> 21:18.560
I mean, Auntie.

458
21:20.470 --> 21:22.160
You might as well tell me that tomorrow, Jane.

459
21:23.200 --> 21:25.600
My parents are taking care of some business overseas.

460
21:25.860 --> 21:28.120
Oh, I was going to ask.

461
21:28.230 --> 21:30.720
You know that your parents are away right now,

462
21:30.910 --> 21:32.120
so what brings you home?

463
21:32.470 --> 21:34.680
I know that nobody is here,

464
21:34.700 --> 21:36.280
so I want to keep you company.

465
21:37.100 --> 21:39.490
I don't want to be alone for too long.

466
21:40.080 --> 21:42.620
Aww...

467
21:42.710 --> 21:45.250
My boy is such a sweetheart.

468
21:45.270 --> 21:47.330
Why are you so, so sweet?

469
21:47.350 --> 21:49.000
Come here. Let me give you a smooch.

470
21:49.640 --> 21:50.440
Come here.

471
21:52.130 --> 21:54.740
Do you know how much I missed you, Master Jane?

472
21:58.490 --> 22:01.260
Jaab, you're staying at this tiny house, okay?

473
22:04.050 --> 22:06.190
As you wish, Master Jane.

474
22:07.430 --> 22:08.920
I'm not as classy as you, Master Attajiranont.

475
22:09.520 --> 22:10.680
Wait, hey...

476
22:10.870 --> 22:13.360
Have you been looking through my family background or what?

477
22:14.000 --> 22:15.020
Khanoon told me.

478
22:16.780 --> 22:18.050
What did he say?

479
22:18.070 --> 22:19.320
He said that

480
22:19.580 --> 22:21.640
your face doesn't match your last name at all.

481
22:22.780 --> 22:24.520
So people don't believe that you're rich.

482
22:29.930 --> 22:31.280
Is he taking a shot at me?

483
22:31.840 --> 22:33.960
Hey, Jane. Wait up!

484
22:34.060 --> 22:34.820
Jane!

485
22:35.550 --> 22:36.460
Wait for me.

486
22:41.210 --> 22:42.520
Whoa...

487
22:47.760 --> 22:48.920
Oh, Jane.

488
22:48.960 --> 22:50.280
Your place is stunning.

489
22:50.820 --> 22:52.480
I can tell a lot of work has gone into it.

490
22:53.230 --> 22:54.970
Dad designed everything himself.

491
22:55.400 --> 22:57.640
But it's mostly what Mom likes.

492
22:57.820 --> 22:59.920
Whoa, how romantic...

493
23:01.540 --> 23:02.970
The weather's really good here at night.

494
23:02.990 --> 23:05.280
I like sleeping here inside the mosquito net with the windows open.

495
23:05.700 --> 23:07.580
But if this isn't up your alley,

496
23:08.720 --> 23:09.400
just turn the A/C on.

497
23:09.870 --> 23:10.660
Okay.

498
23:11.460 --> 23:12.120
Well then...

499
23:12.400 --> 23:13.490
do make yourself at home.

500
23:13.910 --> 23:15.550
Any spot here can be an isolated corner

501
23:15.570 --> 23:16.980
for your work.

502
23:17.220 --> 23:18.000
Don't hold back.

503
23:18.720 --> 23:19.580
Right.

504
23:32.180 --> 23:34.670
Had I met Jane back in my university days,

505
23:34.690 --> 23:38.840
I would've gotten a better grade in chemistry analysis.

506
23:39.620 --> 23:41.690
When it comes to the chemistry between two people,

507
23:41.720 --> 23:45.180
not only does it make one's heart erupt,

508
23:45.360 --> 23:48.000
but it also turns something mundane

509
23:48.100 --> 23:50.800
into something extraordinarily special like Mek said.

510
23:51.050 --> 23:53.120
I don't know if Jane feels the same,

511
23:55.040 --> 23:57.700
but I have to thank him for making me feel this much.

512
24:04.200 --> 24:05.890
[SCENE 1: INT. GARDEN HOUSE - DAY]

513
24:05.910 --> 24:07.600
[CHARACTERS]

514
24:17.410 --> 24:18.210
Oh, oh.

515
24:19.260 --> 24:22.000
Why don't you rest on the pillow, Master?

516
24:22.550 --> 24:24.750
I prefer your lap.

517
24:25.710 --> 24:26.900
Goodness!

518
24:27.380 --> 24:27.990
Oh,

519
24:28.560 --> 24:30.760
what has Bangkok done to my boy?

520
24:30.780 --> 24:31.480
Hm?

521
24:45.640 --> 24:47.710
That's what my seniors at the company like to say,

522
24:47.730 --> 24:49.070
so I picked it up from them.

523
24:49.090 --> 24:50.750
Oh!

524
24:52.230 --> 24:54.570
What about your friend?

525
24:55.080 --> 24:56.650
What brings him here

526
24:56.670 --> 24:58.810
on the same trip?

527
25:00.580 --> 25:02.680
His name is Jaab.

528
25:04.280 --> 25:05.500
He's my colleague.

529
25:06.010 --> 25:07.250
We sit next to each other.

530
25:23.810 --> 25:25.480
Jaab is big and tall.

531
25:26.560 --> 25:28.750
The more he frowns, the scarier he looks.

532
25:29.270 --> 25:30.780
But I gave everything I had

533
25:30.950 --> 25:32.650
to start a conversation with him.

534
25:33.390 --> 25:34.160
Hello.

535
25:36.710 --> 25:37.540
I'm Jane.

536
25:38.080 --> 25:39.510
It's my first day here.

537
25:43.460 --> 25:44.250
I'm Jaab.

538
25:53.680 --> 25:55.930
The flea market opens at noon.

539
25:55.950 --> 25:57.360
Do you want to go together?

540
25:57.930 --> 25:59.200
I brought my own lunch.

541
25:59.510 --> 26:00.310
Oh.

542
26:00.790 --> 26:02.000
That's okay.

543
26:14.260 --> 26:15.210
Hello, Jane.

544
26:16.220 --> 26:16.780
Hi.

545
26:16.800 --> 26:17.440
Hi...

546
26:24.110 --> 26:24.840
I'm here...

547
26:25.150 --> 26:26.120
to get some apples.

548
26:26.230 --> 26:27.700
I found out later

549
26:27.720 --> 26:29.050
after talking to Min that

550
26:29.390 --> 26:32.310
the first impression Jaab put so much effort into making

551
26:32.770 --> 26:35.270
was completely ruined by me.

552
26:39.150 --> 26:40.080
Hi, Jaab.

553
26:41.470 --> 26:42.160
Hello, Jane.

554
26:44.520 --> 26:46.030
And what happened next?

555
26:46.050 --> 26:48.000
How did you two become close?

556
26:49.310 --> 26:50.360
Mm...

557
26:50.570 --> 26:52.410
It was probably back when...

558
26:53.270 --> 26:54.910
I started a conversation with him.

559
26:54.930 --> 26:56.000
Wait for me, please.

560
26:57.990 --> 27:00.400
- Then it was just us in the same elevator. - Hi, Jaab.

561
27:01.070 --> 27:02.080
Hello, Jane.

562
27:04.920 --> 27:05.530
And...

563
27:05.860 --> 27:08.470
- time didn't fly by too slowly there... - Want some dough sticks?

564
27:09.990 --> 27:11.550
like it does whenever I'm with the others.

565
27:17.140 --> 27:17.890
Want some more?

566
27:21.710 --> 27:24.350
Before I knew it, we'd grown close.

567
27:26.160 --> 27:28.710
Did you tell Min about all of this?

568
27:29.450 --> 27:30.650
If she finds out,

569
27:31.000 --> 27:31.850
I believe that

570
27:32.250 --> 27:34.280
she must be really happy for you.

571
27:35.720 --> 27:36.790
I've been busy,

572
27:37.160 --> 27:38.270
and so has she.

573
27:38.440 --> 27:39.960
So we haven't been in touch.

574
27:40.120 --> 27:41.950
And with Jaab...

575
27:42.710 --> 27:43.330
Well...

576
27:43.950 --> 27:45.750
We've been growing closer.

577
27:46.300 --> 27:49.390
We've gotten so used to each other that...

578
27:49.470 --> 27:50.480
there's no point in sharing.

579
27:51.980 --> 27:53.320
That's great.

580
27:55.870 --> 27:58.260
I've never imagined that

581
27:58.470 --> 28:00.880
I'd have another close friend aside from Min.

582
28:03.890 --> 28:04.440
Alright.

583
28:04.460 --> 28:05.750
Now that you're lying down,

584
28:05.780 --> 28:07.220
I guess I have to feed you like this.

585
28:11.590 --> 28:12.290
Oh!

586
28:13.310 --> 28:14.680
As delicious as always.

587
28:14.770 --> 28:15.750
It's from the same mango tree.

588
28:15.770 --> 28:17.350
Why wouldn't it taste the same?

589
28:27.730 --> 28:28.320
Oh?

590
28:29.100 --> 28:29.870
Jane!

591
28:30.150 --> 28:31.080
What are you doing?!

592
28:31.420 --> 28:32.680
I'm on my way to watch the sunset.

593
28:32.810 --> 28:34.110
Oh, and where are you...

594
28:34.640 --> 28:36.040
taking the motorbike?

595
28:37.200 --> 28:38.100
Oh.

596
28:38.120 --> 28:40.000
It's old now, and it gets loud when it runs.

597
28:40.170 --> 28:41.840
I'm afraid the sound might disturb you while you work.

598
28:41.860 --> 28:43.720
So I'll start the engine far away from here.

599
28:44.800 --> 28:45.720
Oh, really?

600
28:46.020 --> 28:46.600
And...

601
28:47.080 --> 28:48.920
Where are you watching the sunset?

602
28:49.450 --> 28:50.280
Around here somewhere.

603
28:50.430 --> 28:51.640
Dad never allows me to go far.

604
28:52.880 --> 28:53.880
You look like

605
28:54.030 --> 28:55.400
someone who can't ride a motorbike.

606
28:55.700 --> 28:56.750
Can you really?

607
29:01.210 --> 29:01.800
Jane!

608
29:02.000 --> 29:04.630
Let's go!

609
29:04.900 --> 29:06.680
Woo-hoo!

610
29:08.930 --> 29:09.640
Jane,

611
29:10.080 --> 29:11.880
your place is super stunning.

612
29:12.330 --> 29:13.670
- So is that spot. - Whoa, Jane.

613
29:13.690 --> 29:14.570
There, there.

614
29:14.590 --> 29:15.600
I want to go there, Jane.

615
29:15.960 --> 29:16.850
Let's go.

616
29:43.090 --> 29:44.340
Jane, you're so mean.

617
29:46.250 --> 29:46.970
Me?

618
29:47.460 --> 29:48.320
How exactly?

619
29:50.380 --> 29:51.590
You know a place this stunning,

620
29:51.740 --> 29:53.050
but you kept it all to yourself.

621
29:53.810 --> 29:55.380
You've never asked if I wanted to tag along.

622
29:59.430 --> 30:00.890
When you work,

623
30:00.910 --> 30:02.640
you like to be alone

624
30:02.660 --> 30:05.040
quietly in an isolated corner.

625
30:07.030 --> 30:09.620
Oh, you do care!

626
30:09.850 --> 30:12.300
You remember everything about me.

627
30:13.500 --> 30:15.470
Bew knows that you're here at my place.

628
30:16.010 --> 30:18.660
If you returned empty-handed,

629
30:19.120 --> 30:20.850
she would probably scold me as well.

630
30:22.780 --> 30:23.890
Oh, Jane.

631
30:24.380 --> 30:25.450
You ruined the mood.

632
30:27.140 --> 30:27.980
By the way,

633
30:28.500 --> 30:29.570
is this your usual spot?

634
30:31.080 --> 30:31.660
Mm.

635
30:32.050 --> 30:34.250
I came here every day before my university years.

636
30:34.940 --> 30:36.120
It was part of my routine.

637
30:39.730 --> 30:40.880
Tell me about it.

638
30:41.660 --> 30:42.250
Hm?

639
30:42.950 --> 30:43.610
Well...

640
30:44.120 --> 30:45.200
Tell me anything

641
30:46.310 --> 30:47.710
that happened before we met.

642
30:51.790 --> 30:54.200
I grew up with the farm and the orchards here.

643
30:55.250 --> 30:57.430
I was homeschooled here, too.

644
30:59.400 --> 31:02.480
My first big community was at the university.

645
31:03.640 --> 31:04.520
Then...

646
31:05.070 --> 31:06.440
I found myself a close friend.

647
31:07.120 --> 31:08.160
Her name is Min.

648
31:09.310 --> 31:10.040
Min...

649
31:12.440 --> 31:15.600
The company is my second big community.

650
31:17.110 --> 31:18.590
And I found myself another close friend.

651
31:19.790 --> 31:21.330
His name is Jaab.

652
31:28.320 --> 31:29.620
It's my pleasure.

653
31:39.230 --> 31:41.590
His world is something unknown to me.

654
31:43.510 --> 31:45.490
However, it answers the question I had.

655
31:46.090 --> 31:48.300
What turned him into someone...

656
31:51.740 --> 31:53.840
who is like a part of the sky,

657
31:56.110 --> 31:57.210
the clouds,

658
31:58.740 --> 32:00.160
and the sunlight?

659
32:01.880 --> 32:04.010
It's something beautiful and warm,

660
32:09.940 --> 32:11.430
yet at the same time,

661
32:17.760 --> 32:18.780
there appears to be a fine line

662
32:18.800 --> 32:20.800
between the two of us.

663
32:23.610 --> 32:24.280
Oh!

664
32:25.720 --> 32:26.440
Jane.

665
32:27.770 --> 32:29.520
Stop it, Jane.

666
32:30.710 --> 32:31.590
Jane, Jane.

667
32:31.610 --> 32:32.540
Jane! Jane!

668
32:32.560 --> 32:33.300
No, no.

669
32:33.320 --> 32:34.320
Jane, please.

670
32:37.660 --> 32:38.390
Jane. Cut, cut.

671
32:38.410 --> 32:39.540
Cut, cut, cut.

672
32:39.800 --> 32:41.160
Cut, cut. No, please, Jane.

673
32:42.780 --> 32:44.240
Jane, take it easy.

674
32:44.260 --> 32:46.300
Jane, no, no.

675
32:47.070 --> 32:48.720
Jane, Jane, Jane!

676
32:50.330 --> 32:51.960
When the male lead is about to make a move,

677
32:52.710 --> 32:54.360
it's like he's always pushed back

678
32:55.050 --> 32:56.970
to the point where he starts wondering...

679
32:57.330 --> 32:59.280
whether he should stop or keep going.

680
32:59.300 --> 33:00.600
Mm...

681
33:00.710 --> 33:02.260
The idea itself sounds interesting.

682
33:02.280 --> 33:04.250
But are you sure that you listened to the right song?

683
33:05.540 --> 33:07.740
The crux of the story is...

684
33:07.760 --> 33:09.110
a fallout of a relationship.

685
33:09.400 --> 33:11.760
It's not being lost in love.

686
33:13.740 --> 33:15.860
I'm out of the loop,

687
33:15.880 --> 33:17.200
but I can tell he's very invested.

688
33:17.620 --> 33:19.520
Is there anything you'd like to confess?

689
33:20.930 --> 33:21.580
Hm?

690
33:22.340 --> 33:23.160
No!

691
33:23.480 --> 33:24.080
Well...

692
33:24.420 --> 33:26.400
This is how I operate.

693
33:26.580 --> 33:27.850
It's method acting, you see.

694
33:27.970 --> 33:29.440
But you're the director,

695
33:29.460 --> 33:30.380
not an actor.

696
33:30.400 --> 33:32.080
Acting, my ass.

697
33:32.210 --> 33:33.250
Fine, fine.

698
33:34.080 --> 33:36.110
So my idea hasn't hit the mark.

699
33:36.920 --> 33:37.750
But...

700
33:37.910 --> 33:39.320
I've still got time.

701
33:39.420 --> 33:40.740
Let me take some time to rethink.

702
33:40.760 --> 33:41.480
And then what?

703
33:42.060 --> 33:43.760
Are you going to stop here or keep going?

704
33:45.230 --> 33:47.550
I don't know either, but...

705
33:48.450 --> 33:49.970
Oh, you bastards!

706
33:49.990 --> 33:51.770
Both of you are fuckers!

707
33:51.790 --> 33:53.410
- Fuck you! - I'm a bastard,

708
33:53.430 --> 33:54.380
just like you.

709
33:54.400 --> 33:55.610
- That's why we're friends. - Ugh...

710
33:55.630 --> 33:57.390
I'm the tiniest bastard here, then.

711
33:57.410 --> 33:58.720
Plus, I'm the most handsome one.

712
33:58.740 --> 33:59.720
So what, huh?

713
33:59.750 --> 34:00.680
So... Oh!

714
34:03.590 --> 34:05.640
The bites of the mosquitoes here are a bit less painful than a tiger's.

715
34:13.570 --> 34:14.630
You're on your phone?

716
34:15.380 --> 34:16.520
I'm sorry. I didn't notice.

717
34:16.770 --> 34:17.500
Oh.

718
34:18.060 --> 34:19.320
It's okay, Jane...

719
34:19.440 --> 34:20.320
By the way...

720
34:21.230 --> 34:22.550
How did you know that?

721
34:22.990 --> 34:24.120
Have you been bitten by a tiger before?

722
34:29.550 --> 34:30.850
Hey, Jane.

723
34:31.730 --> 34:33.320
Did I upset you in some way?

724
34:35.780 --> 34:37.120
The tiger wouldn't dare bite me.

725
34:38.350 --> 34:39.840
But it once broke into the orchard.

726
34:40.080 --> 34:41.010
What?!

727
34:41.580 --> 34:42.820
- I'm serious. - Where, Jane?

728
34:43.340 --> 34:44.360
I saw it with my own eyes.

729
34:44.600 --> 34:45.840
It was gigantic.

730
34:46.580 --> 34:48.090
It was very intimidating, too.

731
34:49.030 --> 34:50.240
And it was...

732
34:50.280 --> 34:51.160
What?

733
34:52.900 --> 34:54.760
It was bouncing around on its tail.

734
34:54.920 --> 34:56.090
Was it, Jane?!

735
34:56.640 --> 34:57.420
And...

736
34:58.330 --> 35:00.100
the tiger was friends with a yellow bear

737
35:00.590 --> 35:01.840
and a pink piglet.

738
35:02.180 --> 35:03.000
Am I right?

739
35:04.000 --> 35:05.160
The tiger you're talking about...

740
35:06.310 --> 35:07.060
Ow!

741
35:08.610 --> 35:09.980
Are you teasing me?

742
35:10.000 --> 35:12.470
- Are you, Jane? - Ow, you're squeezing my cheeks again.

743
35:12.490 --> 35:13.550
Oh, so what?

744
35:14.810 --> 35:15.920
- Take that. - Ow, ow.

745
35:16.890 --> 35:18.020
What are you doing, Jane?

746
35:23.100 --> 35:23.880
I'm squeezing yours.

747
35:23.900 --> 35:24.880
There, there, there.

748
35:24.920 --> 35:26.730
I want to know what makes it fun,

749
35:26.750 --> 35:28.160
and why you like squeezing my cheeks so much.

750
35:28.340 --> 35:29.240
Come on, then.

751
35:29.320 --> 35:29.960
Then...

752
35:30.100 --> 35:32.080
Whoever lets go first loses. Deal?

753
35:32.100 --> 35:33.240
Okay.

754
35:33.280 --> 35:34.060
Come on.

755
35:45.900 --> 35:47.620
- Come here. Come here. - Bring it on.

756
36:05.270 --> 36:05.930
Jane.

757
36:10.890 --> 36:11.650
I...

758
36:14.440 --> 36:15.790
like...

759
36:16.540 --> 36:17.820
Dinner is ready, dear.

760
36:17.840 --> 36:19.730
The stir-fried chayote is nice and hot.

761
36:19.750 --> 36:21.400
stir-fried chayote very much!

762
36:25.580 --> 36:26.360
Really?

763
36:27.880 --> 36:29.880
You like stir-fried chayote?

764
36:30.220 --> 36:31.960
Do you know that chayote

765
36:31.980 --> 36:33.040
is my favorite?

766
36:33.540 --> 36:35.880
Auntie Kaew makes the best stir-fried chayote.

767
36:36.890 --> 36:38.280
I want you to try.

768
36:38.340 --> 36:39.010
Shall we?

769
36:39.330 --> 36:39.930
Mm.

770
36:40.270 --> 36:40.770
Come on.

771
36:41.780 --> 36:42.560
Let's go.

772
36:51.120 --> 36:52.760
What the hell is stir-fried chayote?

773
36:53.990 --> 36:55.190
Damn it, Jaab.

774
36:55.210 --> 36:56.620
You fucking idiot!

775
36:56.640 --> 36:59.160
- Jaab, are you coming or not? - I am!

776
37:04.310 --> 37:05.920
Here you go.

777
37:06.640 --> 37:08.590
Here, stir-fried chayote.

778
37:09.280 --> 37:11.390
I kept the food pretty mild.

779
37:11.410 --> 37:13.760
I didn't know how much chili you could handle.

780
37:17.420 --> 37:18.080
Oh...

781
37:19.730 --> 37:21.620
A little spicy is fine, Auntie Kaew.

782
37:22.600 --> 37:23.980
Perfect. Well then...

783
37:24.000 --> 37:25.980
please go take a shower right after you're finished,

784
37:26.000 --> 37:27.520
because it gets very cold late at night.

785
37:27.930 --> 37:29.720
Then come have some chilled longan in syrup.

786
37:29.790 --> 37:30.700
I made some for you.

787
37:30.720 --> 37:32.240
It's in the fridge, very chilled.

788
37:32.410 --> 37:33.460
Oh, Auntie Kaew.

789
37:33.820 --> 37:34.840
Thank you very much!

790
37:35.720 --> 37:37.560
Eat well. Enjoy.

791
37:37.580 --> 37:38.320
Thank you.

792
37:41.770 --> 37:43.440
Some stir-fried chayote for you.

793
37:43.870 --> 37:44.840
Eat up,

794
37:45.060 --> 37:45.820
Master Jaab.

795
37:46.860 --> 37:48.540
I'm not a kid, alright?

796
37:51.400 --> 37:52.170
Whoa!

797
37:55.290 --> 37:56.600
This is incredible, Jane.

798
38:00.680 --> 38:01.800
They are all incredible.

799
38:02.170 --> 38:03.050
Whoa...

800
38:06.960 --> 38:07.980
What are you looking at, Master Jane?

801
38:09.120 --> 38:10.480
Jaab, you chubby kid.

802
38:10.920 --> 38:11.550
What?

803
38:12.600 --> 38:14.090
Don't take a shot at me

804
38:14.590 --> 38:16.240
if you haven't seen my six-pack.

805
39:20.600 --> 39:21.400
Oh!

806
39:35.560 --> 39:37.560
[SCENE 1: INT. GARDEN HOUSE - DAY] [CHARACTERS: CUTE]

807
39:37.650 --> 39:38.120
Whoa.

808
39:39.420 --> 39:40.590
What the fuck did I just type?

809
39:42.960 --> 39:44.840
You've totally lost it, Jaab...

810
39:50.700 --> 39:53.880
[JANE would like to share a photo]

811
39:58.930 --> 40:00.040
[Accept]

812
40:00.060 --> 40:00.900
What is it?

813
40:01.600 --> 40:02.680
[Open Gallery]

814
40:20.640 --> 40:21.500
Oh.

815
40:23.130 --> 40:24.210
Where?

816
40:26.440 --> 40:28.560
You came...?

817
40:29.380 --> 40:31.200
Finally...

818
40:33.400 --> 40:35.640
- Boo! - Ah!

819
40:36.310 --> 40:37.420
Jane!

820
40:37.980 --> 40:38.920
What is this?

821
40:39.640 --> 40:40.890
You scared me.

822
40:43.400 --> 40:44.870
You almost gave me a heart attack.

823
40:50.430 --> 40:52.530
You invited me out for stargazing by sending me a photo?

824
40:52.610 --> 40:53.770
What if I missed the notification?

825
40:55.090 --> 40:56.440
I was afraid that you'd already gone to bed.

826
40:56.860 --> 40:58.240
So I decided to send a photo.

827
40:58.900 --> 41:00.480
If your AirDrop was on,

828
41:00.500 --> 41:02.840
then your laptop would be on, too.

829
41:03.140 --> 41:05.060
Which would mean that you were still up.

830
41:05.800 --> 41:06.570
Jane.

831
41:06.860 --> 41:07.990
Don't complicate things.

832
41:08.340 --> 41:09.720
Just ask me if you want.

833
41:10.050 --> 41:12.840
Even if I were asleep, I would wake up for you.

834
41:19.270 --> 41:20.570
The stars here are beautiful,

835
41:21.360 --> 41:22.820
in case you want to put them in the MV.

836
41:31.790 --> 41:32.570
Whoa!

837
41:32.970 --> 41:34.080
You're right!

838
41:37.870 --> 41:39.060
Jaab, lie down.

839
41:39.160 --> 41:40.380
It's like looking at a giant TV screen.

840
41:40.490 --> 41:41.060
Huh?

841
41:41.120 --> 41:41.980
Come on.

842
41:44.400 --> 41:44.920
Oh.

843
41:51.040 --> 41:52.400
Whoa.

844
41:55.620 --> 41:56.310
Jaab.

845
41:56.800 --> 41:57.470
Hm?

846
41:58.490 --> 42:00.690
Have you ever stargazed in a classroom before?

847
42:02.650 --> 42:04.070
How could that be possible, Jane?

848
42:04.280 --> 42:05.840
A classroom comes with a ceiling.

849
42:08.060 --> 42:08.840
But here,

850
42:10.210 --> 42:11.570
you're doing it right now.

851
42:12.800 --> 42:14.020
This used to be my classroom.

852
42:17.290 --> 42:18.280
You mean...

853
42:18.670 --> 42:20.300
back when you were homeschooled?

854
42:20.590 --> 42:21.130
Mm.

855
42:21.830 --> 42:22.840
I studied here,

856
42:23.390 --> 42:25.040
had lunches here,

857
42:25.470 --> 42:26.590
and played here.

858
42:26.800 --> 42:28.310
I spent all my time here.

859
42:33.400 --> 42:34.220
So...

860
42:34.770 --> 42:36.180
why were you homeschooled?

861
42:36.800 --> 42:38.300
Out of everyone I know,

862
42:38.330 --> 42:39.920
you're the first.

863
42:42.660 --> 42:44.610
I went to a regular school when I was little.

864
42:45.330 --> 42:47.370
But I was small, so I was always picked on.

865
42:48.750 --> 42:50.710
I cried on the way home every day.

866
42:51.520 --> 42:52.820
My parents were worried about me,

867
42:53.620 --> 42:56.440
so they wanted me to do whatever made me happy.

868
42:57.700 --> 42:59.200
And what made me happy

869
42:59.810 --> 43:00.840
was staying home.

870
43:02.660 --> 43:03.390
That's why

871
43:03.650 --> 43:05.140
I was homeschooled.

872
43:08.580 --> 43:09.940
So your classroom

873
43:10.590 --> 43:12.940
has the most beautiful view ever, huh?

874
43:14.440 --> 43:15.080
Yeah.

875
43:36.500 --> 43:37.260
Jaab...

876
43:40.820 --> 43:41.640
Jane...

877
43:51.300 --> 43:52.620
I...

878
43:59.240 --> 44:00.500
like you.

879
44:02.640 --> 44:04.240
I like you, too.

880
44:41.800 --> 44:43.430
Your classroom

881
44:44.080 --> 44:46.600
is probably the most beautiful one in the world, yeah?

882
44:47.840 --> 44:48.440
Mm.

883
44:52.740 --> 44:53.440
I also...

884
44:53.600 --> 44:54.920
said the same thing

885
44:55.540 --> 44:57.710
when I was talking to Min.

886
45:15.850 --> 45:16.600
Ow!

887
45:17.520 --> 45:18.200
Jane!

888
45:18.290 --> 45:19.160
What did you do?!

889
45:19.440 --> 45:20.350
I'm sorry.

890
45:20.940 --> 45:21.810
There was a mosquito.

891
45:24.250 --> 45:27.110
I swear I was being as gentle as I could.

892
45:29.430 --> 45:30.200
Did it hurt?

893
45:30.680 --> 45:31.500
Hold on.

894
45:32.380 --> 45:33.480
What happened?

895
45:33.660 --> 45:35.230
Did I fall asleep?

896
45:35.660 --> 45:36.200
Mm.

897
45:37.870 --> 45:38.560
And...

898
45:38.750 --> 45:39.720
How long was I asleep?

899
45:41.580 --> 45:42.720
A while.

900
45:43.440 --> 45:44.470
And...

901
45:44.520 --> 45:46.320
While I was asleep,

902
45:46.340 --> 45:48.020
did I do something strange?

903
45:49.230 --> 45:51.040
Tell me the truth. I won't get mad.

904
45:53.880 --> 45:54.640
Nothing.

905
45:55.400 --> 45:56.040
Really?

906
45:56.780 --> 45:57.470
Mm.

907
46:10.030 --> 46:11.230
Your life here is so comfortable.

908
46:11.250 --> 46:13.240
Why did you move to Bangkok to work for someone else?

909
46:13.260 --> 46:14.200
I just wanted to see

910
46:14.390 --> 46:16.840
what a starless night sky looked like.

911
46:17.030 --> 46:17.710
I think...

912
46:17.960 --> 46:19.440
I'm gonna make a move on Jane.

913
46:19.460 --> 46:20.440
Jaab has a crush on...

914
46:20.490 --> 46:21.470
- Hey, wait, wait. - Hey, hey!

915
46:21.490 --> 46:22.960
Oh, I...

916
46:23.160 --> 46:24.330
Spending time with you

917
46:24.480 --> 46:26.280
makes my life seem a lot simpler.

918
46:26.300 --> 46:27.800
Stay with me for a long time, okay?

919
46:27.970 --> 46:29.040
Don't leave.

920
46:29.160 --> 46:31.330
If you don't tell me to leave, then I won't.

921
46:31.880 --> 46:33.340
Are you...

922
46:33.400 --> 46:35.800
having a crush on someone?

923
46:36.000 --> 46:37.220
Is it me?!
